# Legacy prototype material — NOT for publication.
# Contains prior-prototype source, internal knowledge docs, and licensed
# third-party datasets. Must never be pushed to this public repo.
legacy/

# Local source library — NOT for publication.
# Copyrighted source PDFs held for local reading and citation only. The
# repo cites and links them; it never reproduces them. Nothing inside is
# ever committed, and the folder sits outside public/ so no build can
# publish it. The trailing slash ignores the directory and all contents.
sources-local/

# Engineer-reference only — NOT for publication.
# Brand and UI specifications. Engineer-eyes-only; never published.
#
# The brand book moved from the repository root into brand/ when version 4
# arrived on 30 Aug 2026. This bare rule has no leading slash, so it matches
# the book at either path, and the brand/* rule below catches it a second
# time. It is ignored twice over and publishes from neither place.
BRAND.md
UI_REFERENCE.md

# Brand assets — ignored EXCEPT the ~~two~~ ~~THREE~~ FOUR files the product actually ships.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# tree is opened level by level and re-closed at each one. Everything else
# under brand/ — the rest of the crew, the other logo colourways, the pixel
# avatars, the design-system export — stays unpublished.
brand/*
!brand/assets/
brand/assets/*
!brand/assets/logo/
brand/assets/logo/*
!brand/assets/logo/wordmark.svg
!brand/assets/bots/
brand/assets/bots/*
!brand/assets/bots/bridget.svg
!brand/assets/bots/phoebe.svg
!brand/assets/bots/calvin.svg
# Wellington hosts the free desk from 2 Sep 2026. Without this line his
# portrait builds locally and fails on deploy — the trap that caught Calvin's.
!brand/assets/bots/wellington.svg

# Design references — engineer-eyes-only, never published.
#
# Saved production pages and mockups, brought in BY THE MAINTAINER'S HAND —
# the calculator page on 1 Sep 2026, the dispatch desk and console on
# 2 Sep 2026 — so the free surfaces and the paid ones read as one family.
# That is the sanctioned route and the only one: rule zero forbids the
# engineer fetching, matching or guessing at the production side, and it is
# unchanged.
#
# They are LOOK references and nothing else — layout, row anatomy, rail and
# chat-box density. Not their data, not their live composers, not
# organisations, roles or saving.
#
# ~~The calculator reference sits at the repository root.~~ Moved inside
# Design refs/ by the maintainer's hand on 2 Sep 2026. The root rule is kept
# in case it is ever dropped there again; it matches nothing today.
Calculator design ref/
Design refs/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
*.local
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment files — NOT for publication.
# The CARTO basemaps key lives here locally and in the deployment platform's
# settings; it is never committed. `.env.local` is already caught by *.local
# above, but a plain `.env` was not, and a key is exactly the thing that ends
# up in one by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Raw source data — downloaded, converted, never committed.
# Only the simplified web-ready outputs in public/ are tracked.
data-src/

# The maintainer's export copies — NOT for publication.
# Shell_B_-prefixed duplicates of the root documents, made at session close so
# they can be carried elsewhere by hand. They are copies, never the source: the
# root files are what binds, and an edit made to a copy is lost. Nothing in the
# build reads this folder.
exports/
